# The image's own entries for the programs that accept connections (LISTENERS in /etc/amethystora/security.conf):
# what the image's own services listen on, which starts when the watcher may already have looked, recorded and
# not said. The machine's own are in /etc/amethystora/allow.d/listeners (ame security allow listeners "PROGRAM
# PORT"). A glob each. The program is the file the listening process runs, in the system's own mount namespace:
# the image's entries name that file, which a process cannot take as it can the name ss shows. An entry of the
# machine's with a name instead of a file still matches that name.
#
# fwupd's passim, which offers the firmware metadata fwupd downloaded to the machines nearby; it starts when
# firmware is looked for, from Updates or GNOME Firmware (P2pPolicy in /etc/fwupd/fwupd.conf)
/usr/libexec/passimd 27500
# The phone link (amethystora-connect), for phones, from the first login, which may come after the watcher's first
# run: the protocol's port 1716, and one port of 1739 to 1764 for a file in transit. The firewall opens them at home
# only (ame security home-networks)
/usr/libexec/amethystora-connect 1716
/usr/libexec/amethystora-connect 173[9]
/usr/libexec/amethystora-connect 174[0-9]
/usr/libexec/amethystora-connect 175[0-9]
/usr/libexec/amethystora-connect 176[0-4]
# Move to this computer (amethystora-move): the new computer's port while `ame system move receive` waits, for ten
# minutes at most. The firewall opens it at home only
/usr/libexec/amethystora-move 4793
# The remote desktop (gnome-remote-desktop-daemon), only while ame desktop help-me or second-screen runs it, on the
# one port the remote-screen switch opens in the home zone (ame security remote-screen)
/usr/libexec/gnome-remote-desktop-daemon 3389

# The store for another computer's backup (R7-35, ame backup store, only while it is on): rclone serving restic, one port of 8767 to 8799 for each computer paired,
# and python3 on 8766 for the three minutes a pairing waits. The firewall opens them at home only (ame security backup-store)
/usr/bin/rclone 87[6-9][0-9]
/usr/bin/python3* 8766
